James inquired about customizing legends in ggplot, specifically needing the fill legend to show colors without patterns overlaid. I suggested using the `guides()` function in combination with `override.aes` to achieve this, explaining how to modify the fill legend to display colors without patterns while maintaining the main plot’s aesthetics. I provided a code snippet that demonstrated the necessary adjustments using ggplot and the ggpattern library. This solution allows for clearer legends without altering the visual presentation of the data in the plot.
